  "conclusion": "The collection-design proposal did not invent \"Rent out\", \"Lease out\", or temporary-use selling. Both activity nodes were already direct children of \"Sell\" in the machine-derived July 15 baseline. Rob then accepted a synonym decision and exact merge that absorbed \"Lease out\" into \"Rent out\". The later collection-design proposal created the \"Sell temporary use\" wrapper and moved the surviving \"Rent out\" node beneath it. The wrapper and move were human-reviewed, while the underlying activity nodes came from the earlier machine-derived ontology.",
